# Logs
#
# ⚠️ ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored `logs/` matches a
# directory named `logs` at ANY depth, which on 2026-09-11 silently swallowed
# `frontend/src/app/teacher/research/logs/` — a real Next.js route. `git add`
# ignored it, `git commit` succeeded, and the feature shipped a nav link to a
# page that was never committed. Nothing failed; that is what made it dangerous.
# The rule was protecting nothing: the only non-vendored match in the tree was
# that route. `scripts/check-app-routes-tracked.sh` now fails the build on any
# untracked route directory, because the next collision will be `build/`,
# `dist/` or `coverage/` and will look just as much like nothing happening.
/logs/
*.log

